<!-- ══ SLIDE 3: TRADITIONAL MARKETS ══ -->
<div class="slide" data-slide="3">
    <div class="blob" style="width:300px;height:300px;top:-60px;right:-60px;background:#1e3a5f;opacity:0.1;"></div>
    <div class="content">
        <div class="reveal label" style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:0.3rem;">Traditional Markets</div>
        <h2 class="reveal" style="font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:clamp(1.4rem,2.8vw,2rem);font-weight:700;margin-bottom:1rem;">Mediterranean and Caribbean: <span style="color:#f59e0b;">Full. Expensive. Exporting Demand.</span></h2>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;">
            <div style="background:rgba(245,158,11,0.04);border:1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.15);border-radius:12px;padding:1.2rem;border-top:2px solid #f59e0b;">
                <div class="reveal label" style="color:#f59e0b;margin-bottom:0.6rem;">Mediterranean · The Saturated Giant</div>
                <p class="reveal" style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.65;margin-bottom:0.9rem;">Seventy percent of the global superyacht fleet converges on the Western Mediterranean each summer. The result is a structural supply crisis that has been building for a decade. Fleet growth runs at 120 to 150 new yachts per year. Berth supply grows at under 1% annually. Environmental regulations, urban density, and physical coastline constraints make expansion technically and politically near-impossible in the primary locations.</p>
                <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:0.4rem;"><span class="label">Key Figures</span><span class="label" style="color:#1e3a5f;">Status</span></div>
                <div class="row"><span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#475569;">24m+ berths available</span><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.4rem;"><span style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:600;">4,500–4,800</span><span class="pill p-neg">Undersupplied</span></div></div>
                <div class="row"><span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#475569;">Yachts at peak weeks</span><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.4rem;"><span style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:600;">5,000+</span><span class="pill p-neg">Overflow</span></div></div>
                <div class="row"><span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#475569;">Annual berth supply growth</span><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.4rem;"><span style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:600;">&lt;1%</span><span class="pill p-neg">Critical</span></div></div>
                <div class="row"><span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#475569;">Refit yards at capacity</span><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.4rem;"><span style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:600;">70% surveyed</span><span class="pill p-neg">Bottleneck</span></div></div>
                <div style="margin-top:0.9rem;padding:0.7rem;background:rgba(245,158,11,0.06);border-radius:6px;border-left:2px solid #f59e0b;">
                    <p style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.6;">The bottleneck is no longer cyclical. It is structural. Every new delivery without a matching berth pushes demand outward.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div style="background:rgba(245,158,11,0.04);border:1px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.15);border-radius:12px;padding:1.2rem;border-top:2px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.45);">
                <div class="reveal label" style="color:#f59e0b;margin-bottom:0.6rem;">Caribbean · Complementary but Consolidating</div>
                <p class="reveal" style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.65;margin-bottom:0.9rem;">The Caribbean captures the Mediterranean overflow each winter, operating on a near-perfect complementary season from November to April. However, the Caribbean is now at its own ceiling in premium locations. Antigua, Saint Martin, the BVI, and the Grenadines have very limited berth expansion potential. New investment is going into asset consolidation and ancillary real estate, not new marina infrastructure. The market is maturing, not growing.</p>
                <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:0.4rem;"><span class="label">Key Figures</span><span class="label" style="color:#1e3a5f;">Status</span></div>
                <div class="row"><span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#475569;">Peak season</span><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.4rem;"><span style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:600;">November–April</span><span class="pill p-neu">Mirrors Med</span></div></div>
                <div class="row"><span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#475569;">Investment trend 2025–26</span><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.4rem;"><span style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:600;">Consolidation</span><span class="pill p-neu">M&amp;A driven</span></div></div>
                <div class="row"><span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#475569;">Global marina transactions 2024</span><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.4rem;"><span style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:600;">~300</span><span class="pill p-blue">Active</span></div></div>
                <div class="row"><span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#475569;">Berth expansion outlook</span><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.4rem;"><span style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:600;">Limited</span><span class="pill p-neg">Constrained</span></div></div>
                <div style="margin-top:0.9rem;padding:0.7rem;background:rgba(245,158,11,0.06);border-radius:6px;border-left:2px solid rgba(245,158,11,0.4);">
                    <p style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.6;">Capital is not flowing into these markets to build new berths. It is flowing out to find the next ones.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal" style="margin-top:0.5rem;font-size:0.58rem;color:#1e293b;text-align:center;">Sources: Marine Online · Mediterranean Superyacht Forum 2025 · Marina World · Caribbean Property Report 2025</div>
    </div>
</div>

<!-- ══ SLIDE 4: GCC + ALTERNATIVES ══ -->
<div class="slide" data-slide="4">
    <div class="blob" style="width:300px;height:300px;top:-60px;right:-60px;background:#0369a1;opacity:0.1;"></div>
    <div class="content">
        <div class="reveal label" style="color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:0.3rem;">Emerging Markets</div>
        <h2 class="reveal" style="font-family:'Playfair Display',serif;font-size:clamp(1.4rem,2.8vw,2rem);font-weight:700;margin-bottom:1rem;">GCC Under Pressure. <span style="color:#38bdf8;">Where Does the Capital Go?</span></h2>
        <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;">
            <div style="background:rgba(248,113,113,0.04);border:1px solid rgba(248,113,113,0.15);border-radius:12px;padding:1.2rem;border-top:2px solid #f87171;">
                <div class="reveal label" style="color:#f87171;margin-bottom:0.6rem;">GCC · The Disrupted Frontrunner</div>
                <p class="reveal" style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.65;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">The Gulf was the obvious answer to Med saturation. The UAE had the infrastructure ambition, the capital, and the winter season aligned with Mediterranean overflow. NMDC won a USD 104m marina contract in Salalah in May 2025. Oman tendered a luxury marina in Quriyat the same month. The momentum was real.</p>
                <p style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.65;margin-bottom:0.75rem;">Then the Iran conflict changed the calculus. US airstrikes on Iranian nuclear facilities in June 2025 triggered a proposed closure of the Strait of Hormuz and a 60% spike in maritime insurance premiums. The GCC now hosts 321 superyachts but the investment pipeline has slowed materially.</p>
                <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-bottom:0.35rem;"><span class="label">Key Metrics</span><span class="label" style="color:#1e3a5f;">Status</span></div>
                <div class="row"><span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#475569;">Superyachts 30m+ in region</span><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.4rem;"><span style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:600;">321 vessels</span><span class="pill p-blue">5.1% global</span></div></div>
                <div class="row"><span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#475569;">Insurance premium surge</span><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.4rem;"><span style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:600;">+60%</span><span class="pill p-neg">Risk elevated</span></div></div>
                <div class="row"><span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#475569;">GCC contract awards 2025</span><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.4rem;"><span style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:600;">–40% YoY</span><span class="pill p-neg">Slowing</span></div></div>
                <div class="row"><span style="font-size:0.75rem;color:#475569;">Oman marina pipeline</span><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0.4rem;"><span style="font-size:0.78rem;font-weight:600;">USD 150m+</span><span class="pill p-neu">Active</span></div></div>
                <div style="margin-top:0.8rem;padding:0.65rem;background:rgba(248,113,113,0.06);border-radius:6px;border-left:2px solid #f87171;">
                    <p style="font-size:0.74rem;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.6;">Capital that was allocated to the Gulf is now looking for alternatives with similar seasons and lower sovereign risk.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div style="background:rgba(74,222,128,0.04);border:1px solid rgba(74,222,128,0.15);border-radius:12px;padding:1.2rem;border-top:2px solid #4ade80;">
                <div class="reveal label" style="color:#4ade80;margin-bottom:0.6rem;">Alternative Receptors · Where GCC Capital Redirects</div>
                <p class="reveal" style="font-size:0.82rem;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.65;margin-bottom:0.8rem;">Three markets are positioned to absorb displaced GCC investment, each with a different risk and return profile.</p>
                <div style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:0.6rem;">
                    <div style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);border-radius:8px;padding:0.7rem 0.9rem;">
                        <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:0.22rem;"><span style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:700;">Southeast Asia</span><span class="pill p-pos">Highest potential</span></div>
                        <p style="font-size:0.72rem;color:#475569;line-height:1.55;">Nov–Apr season overlap with GCC. Under 2,000 quality berths in Thailand. Aviation demand proven. First mover advantage intact.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);border-radius:8px;padding:0.7rem 0.9rem;">
                        <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:0.22rem;"><span style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:700;">East Mediterranean</span><span class="pill p-neu">Medium term</span></div>
                        <p style="font-size:0.72rem;color:#475569;line-height:1.55;">Greece, Turkey, Cyprus developing capacity. Inside the Med ecosystem. Lower logistics risk. Limited upside vs frontier markets.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div style="background:rgba(255,255,255,0.03);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);border-radius:8px;padding:0.7rem 0.9rem;">
                        <div style="display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;margin-bottom:0.22rem;"><span style="font-size:0.72rem;font-weight:700;">Indian Ocean · Maldives</span><span class="pill p-blue">Niche</span></div>
                        <p style="font-size:0.72rem;color:#475569;line-height:1.55;">Ultra-premium demand established. Infrastructure gap real. Regulatory complexity high. Suitable for specialist operators only.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal" style="margin-top:0.5rem;font-size:0.58rem;color:#1e293b;text-align:center;">Sources: NMDC Group · Zawya · China Briefing · Gulf Superyacht Report 2025-26 · Atlantic Council · Politico</div>
